          "short": "$\\dfrac{1}{\\sin^2\\theta}$; $\\cot^2\\theta$; $\\operatorname{cosec}^2\\theta$.",
          "worked": "For $\\sin\\theta\\ne0$, divide the identity in (a) by $\\sin^2\\theta$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\sin^2\\theta}{\\sin^2\\theta}+\\frac{\\cos^2\\theta}{\\sin^2\\theta}&=\\frac{1}{\\sin^2\\theta}\\\\1+\\frac{\\cos^2\\theta}{\\sin^2\\theta}&=\\frac{1}{\\sin^2\\theta}\\\\1+\\cot^2\\theta&=\\operatorname{cosec}^2\\theta.\\end{align*}$$",
